A recent posting reminds me of another minor grumble, and a possible
solution.
It would be nice (IMHO) if the game began with the player in a 'general
stores' with only some gold, to choose his/her kit. The shop is about to
close, so there's little time to hang around using rings of teleport. If
you don't get out when told, the shopkeeper calls the Kops or throws you
out, taking back all unpaid goods. He probably aught to call the Kops if
you misbehave in the shop anyway.
The point of all this is to reduce the wear and tear caused by players
quitting at the start of the game until they get something like their idea
of their character's ideal kit/status. I haven't tried many of the others,
but the Wiz gets a very poor deal. 
Sure, all the items in the shop would have to be known to the player, but
it doesn't have to be a big, well-stocked shop, just enough to increase
the chances of any particular game being played. If you give the player
a scroll of identify(12), that might get around it.

It would also be nice if the inventory could show 
the price of unpaid items. 

The grumble about being unable to distinguish one's pet dog from the
jackals doesn't really hold up. This could also be the case in real life.
NB: if the jackals were called dingoes they'd match their 'd' symbol.

Thanks for the Amulet of Lifesaving! I liked that one. (No spoiler, I
don't like them)

Seems odd, nobody here has mentioned any bugs on V3.0. We're on S*N 3's,
mind you, nobody's survived below dlev 6 yet..

